      "content": "#include \"knn.h\"\n#include <omp.h>\n#include <limits.h>\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    long total_points = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        total_points += groups[i].length;\n    }\n\n    if (total_points == 0 || k <= 0) {\n        return '\\0';\n    }\n\n    float *xs = (float *) malloc(sizeof(float) * total_points);\n    float *ys = (float *) malloc(sizeof(float) * total_points);\n    char *lbls = (char *) malloc(sizeof(char) * total_points);\n\n    long idx = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        Group g = groups[i];\n        for (int j = 0; j < g.length; j++) {\n            xs[idx] = g.points[j].x;\n            ys[idx] = g.points[j].y;\n            lbls[idx] = g.label;\n            idx++;\n        }\n    }\n\n    int nthreads;\n    #pragma omp parallel\n    {\n        #pragma omp single\n        nthreads = omp_get_num_threads();\n    }\n\n    float *all_d = (float *) malloc(sizeof(float) * (size_t)nthreads * k);\n    char *all_l = (char *) malloc(sizeof(char) * (size_t)nthreads * k);\n    int *all_i = (int *) malloc(sizeof(int) * (size_t)nthreads * k);\n\n    #pragma omp parallel\n    {\n        int tid = omp_get_thread_num();\n        float *ld = all_d + (size_t)tid * k;\n        char *ll = all_l + (size_t)tid * k;\n        int *li = all_i + (size_t)tid * k;\n\n        for (int t = 0; t < k; t++) {\n            ld[t] = -1.0f;\n            ll[t] = (char)-1;\n            li[t] = -1;\n        }\n\n        #pragma omp for schedule(static)\n        for (long i = 0; i < total_points; i++) {\n            float dx = xs[i] - to_evaluate.x;\n            float dy = ys[i] - to_evaluate.y;\n            float d = dx * dx + dy * dy;\n\n            int pos = -1;\n            for (int x = 0; x < k; x++) {\n                if (d < ld[x] || ld[x] == -1.0f) {\n                    pos = x;\n                    break;\n                }\n            }\n\n            if (pos >= 0) {\n                for (int y = k - 1; y > pos; y--) {\n                    ld[y] = ld[y - 1];\n                    ll[y] = ll[y - 1];\n                    li[y] = li[y - 1];\n                }\n                ld[pos] = d;\n                ll[pos] = lbls[i];\n                li[pos] = (int)i;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    float *fd = (float *) malloc(sizeof(float) * k);\n    char *fl = (char *) malloc(sizeof(char) * k);\n    int *fi = (int *) malloc(sizeof(int) * k);\n\n    for (int t = 0; t < k; t++) {\n        fd[t] = -1.0f;\n        fl[t] = (char)-1;\n        fi[t] = -1;\n    }\n\n    int *cur = (int *) calloc(nthreads, sizeof(int));\n    int filled = 0;\n\n    while (filled < k) {\n        int best_t = -1;\n        float best_d = 0.0f;\n        int best_i = INT_MAX;\n\n        for (int t = 0; t < nthreads; t++) {\n            if (cur[t] >= k) continue;\n            float d = all_d[(size_t)t * k + cur[t]];\n            if (d == -1.0f) continue;\n            int idx = all_i[(size_t)t * k + cur[t]];\n            if (best_t == -1 || d < best_d || (d == best_d && idx < best_i)) {\n                best_t = t;\n                best_d = d;\n                best_i = idx;\n            }\n        }\n\n        if (best_t == -1) break;\n\n        fd[filled] = all_d[(size_t)best_t * k + cur[best_t]];\n        fl[filled] = all_l[(size_t)best_t * k + cur[best_t]];\n        fi[filled] = best_i;\n        cur[best_t]++;\n        filled++;\n    }\n\n    qsort(fl, filled, sizeof(char), compare_for_sort);\n\n    char most_frequent = fl[0];\n    int most_frequent_count = 1;\n    int current_frequency = 1;\n\n    for (int i = 1; i < filled; i++) {\n        if (fl[i] != fl[i - 1]) {\n            if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n                most_frequent = fl[i - 1];\n                most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n            }\n            current_frequency = 1;\n        } else {\n            current_frequency++;\n        }\n\n        if (i == filled - 1 && current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n            most_frequent = fl[i - 1];\n            most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n        }\n    }\n\n    free(xs);\n    free(ys);\n    free(lbls);\n    free(all_d);\n    free(all_l);\n    free(all_i);\n    free(fd);\n    free(fl);\n    free(fi);\n    free(cur);\n\n    return most_frequent;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\n    \n    Group * groups = (Group *) malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\n    }\n\n    int k = parse_k();\n\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\n\n    printf(\"%c\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        free(groups[i].points);\n    }\n    free(groups);\n\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/knn.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Parallelizing the k-nearest neighbor selection across all points using OpenMP static work sharing with per-thread private top-k lists and a deterministic merge by (distance, original index) will reduce runtime while preserving exact sequential tie-breaking semantics.",
  "notes": "Only src/knn.c is modified. The header remains unchanged; parsing and compare_for_sort are reused from knn.h. Points are flattened into contiguous arrays to enable a simple parallel loop with schedule(static). Each thread maintains its own top-k list using the same insertion logic as the sequential reference, storing original indices for deterministic tie-breaking during merge. The final majority computation is identical to the baseline.",
